There is no particular relationship between scrolls and spells of th 
same name, beyond their effects.  Evidently it is easier to invent a 
scroll that self-destructs than a spell that can be used repeated by a 
caster using up nothing but manna and (maybe) food.

I think Wizards have a fair chance of writing a spellbook that they have 
never seen before.  (I presume that one needs to have good luck and a 
high level to do so.)

